   <notesStmt>
    <note type="project" target="#dat1">Whitman's note at the bottom of this manuscript implies that he sent the poem to the editors at the <hi rend="italic">Herald</hi> on or before 18 February 1888. Because he was under contract to produce ten poems each month for the paper (see <hi rend="italic">With Walt Whitman in Camden</hi> [Boston: Small, Maynard &amp; Company, 1906] <ref target="med.00001.019">1:41&#8211;42</ref>), most of the poems he published there appear to have been written quickly, with few drafts and light revision. The present manuscript therefore probably dates to the first weeks of February 1888.</note>
     <note type="work_relations" target="xxx.00372" cert="high">
      <p>"The Dismantled Ship" was first published in the 23 February 1888 issue of the <hi rend="italic">New York Herald</hi>. </p>
     </note>
   </notesStmt>
